WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
From process data to editable drawings, then independent assessment.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Start with the process data. Follow these two equipment nodes: their directed connection in the input must also appear in the drawing.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Now watch the saved drawing assemble. Equipment symbols appear first, then routed connections and labels. The animation reveals the actual exported geometry.

4
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.000
This process spans thirty-three drawing sheets. Local layouts must remain connected as one process.

5
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Follow stream S one twenty. It leaves sheet one oh four and continues on sheet one fourteen. The same identifier connects both ends.

6
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Bench reads the delivered CAD independently. These ten objects come from its recorded extraction. The candidate graph is frozen before comparison with the task.

7
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Four scores describe different properties: equipment inventory, symbol geometry, matched connectivity and local layout. These are the recorded scores for this exact drawing package.

8
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Explore the drawings and score evidence on the project website.
